          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            Given an extensional relation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ≺
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \prec
            on a set, two elements are equal if they cannot be distinguished by the structure of the set of elements that they are related to, that those elements are related to, and so on forever in one direction. We generally think of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo ≺
                  %mi y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \prec y
            as saying that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            is a ‘member’ of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ≺
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \prec
            is extensional when “
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            is determined by its members” as in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom+of+extensionality"} axiom of extensionality
            for material
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set+theory"} set theory
          %h2#definitions Definitions
          %p
            We begin with the historically first definition, which is correct for
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/well-founded+relations"} well-founded relations
          %h3#weak_extensionality Weak extensionality
          %p
            A relation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ≺
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \prec
            on a set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            is
            %strong weakly extensional
            if, given any elements
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo =
                  %mi y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x = y
            whenever (for all
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi t
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi t
                  %mo ≺
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t \prec x
            if and only if
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi t
                    %mo ≺
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t \prec y
          %p
            Interpreting
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ≺
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \prec
            as membership
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ∈
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom+of+extensionality"} axiom of extensionality
            as usually stated for
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pure+sets"} pure sets
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ≺
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \prec
            is
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/well-founded+relation"} well-founded
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom+of+foundation"} axiom of foundation
          %p
            However, when
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ≺
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \prec
            is well-founded, weak extensionality is equivalent to all the stronger notions below; thus in that case it is usually called just
            = succeed "." do
              %strong extensionality
          %h3#finsler_extensionality Finsler extensionality
          %p
            Let
